{"version":"1","id":"openssl","handle":"openssl","name":"OpenSSL","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/56836227f9784e529fc1fdd5db066843","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.2371,"y":-3.2806,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":60,"newest_post_at":"2024-07-18T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-12-21T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.016667,"avg_read_time":1.883333,"summary_length_avg":268.916667,"title_length_avg":39.683333,"title_length_var":257.049722,"tag_entropy":2.166601,"tag_diversity":0.466667,"top_tag_share":0.283333,"avg_upvotes":0.033333,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.333333,"zero_engagement_share":0.983333,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.765939,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.176471},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.8235,-8.8971],"cadence_depth":[-3.25,-7.8971],"hype_variety":[-9.5,-8.3824],"title_style":[-0.0441,-6.7647]},"top_tags":[["cryptography",52],["security",28],["open-source",8],["community",4],["github",3],["cyber",3],["tools",3],["performance",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["OpenSSL Is Hiring","OSTIF and Trail of Bits Complete Audit of OpenSSL","OpenSSL 3.1 Release Candidate"],"outlier":["OpenSSL Is Looking to Contract a Full-time Community Engagement Leader / Evangelist"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"AV97QIEPH","title":"Join Our Exclusive Webinar on Performance Tuning and Fetching With OpenSSL","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/07/18/August-Webinar/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/join-our-exclusive-webinar-on-performance-tuning-and-fetching-with-openssl-av97qieph","summary":"Join an insightful webinar on August 1, 2024, to learn key techniques for optimizing application performance using OpenSSL. Topics covered will include efficient OpenSSL configuration, maximizing performance with EVP API, TLS optimization, and real-life case studies. A live Q&A session with experts will be available post-presentation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"xJ3jos18n","title":"OpenSSL Mailing Lists Are Moving to Google Groups","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/07/17/google-groups/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/openssl-mailing-lists-are-moving-to-google-groups-xj3jos18n","summary":"OpenSSL is transitioning its mailing lists to Google Groups effective August 1st, 2024, to enhance collaboration, simplify management, and improve accessibility. Current subscribers will be automatically migrated and will receive invitations to join the corresponding Google Groups. Archives on mta.openssl.org will remain available but not updated.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0_ODbtD2--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2008","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-07-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"x6xnWGjsM","title":"Large Issue Cleanup in OpenSSL","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/06/25/issue-cleanup/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/large-issue-cleanup-in-openssl-x6xnwgjsm","summary":"OpenSSL is addressing its backlog of nearly 2000 outstanding issues by marking older, inactive ones with a label and planning to close them by the end of the 3.4 development cycle. Issues are deemed inactive if they have had no updates for over a year, been fixed but left open, or lack a clear goal. Users can contest the inactive status, continue work on the issue, submit a PR, or let it close automatically with the option to reopen later.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"oO4rMYxHU","title":"New OpenSSL Patch Releases Available","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/06/04/patch-releases-available/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-openssl-patch-releases-available-oo4rmyxhu","summary":"New OpenSSL patch releases are available, including notable changes such as fixes for memory leaks, bug fixes, and security updates.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-04T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"K66E1ZtS4","title":"Soliciting Input Regarding a Potential Hardening Effort","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/06/03/soliciting-input-on-a-hardening-effort/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/soliciting-input-regarding-a-potential-hardening-effort-k66e1zts4","summary":"OpenSSL is seeking input on a potential hardening effort for their library due to an issue related to SIMD registers in memory copy operations. While it is not a security issue requiring immediate action, the community's opinion is being sought to guide efforts on addressing the issue.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-06-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"MsHaSYJ5x","title":"Upcoming Webinar: Getting Started With QUIC and OpenSSL","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/05/28/QUIC-Webinar/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/upcoming-webinar-getting-started-with-quic-and-openssl-mshasyj5x","summary":"Upcoming webinar on getting started with QUIC and OpenSSL. Learn about QUIC basics, implementing a client with QUIC OpenSSL API, and monitoring performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-28T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"dx6xMYwUq","title":"OpenSSL Is Hiring","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/05/26/openssl-is-hiring/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/openssl-is-hiring-dx6xmywuq","summary":"OpenSSL is hiring a mid-level engineer to join their team. The position is remote and the responsibilities include contributing to the development of the OpenSSL toolkit, collaborating on secure software solutions, and maintaining technical documentation. Solid C programming experience and knowledge of network programming concepts are required. To apply, send your resume to jobs@openssl.org.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Nw9zt3a5P","title":"OSTIF and Trail of Bits Complete Audit of OpenSSL","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/05/02/ostif/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ostif-and-trail-of-bits-complete-audit-of-openssl-nw9zt3a5p","summary":"A recent security audit on the OpenSSL software library was conducted by Trail of Bits, funded by OSTIF, resulting in 24 findings with security impact, the addition of 4 fuzzers, and a codebase maturity evaluation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"FSn3fVG7p","title":"Releases Distribution Changes","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/04/30/releases-distribution-changes/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/releases-distribution-changes-fsn3fvg7p","summary":"OpenSSL is simplifying its releases distribution by phasing out older methods and using GitHub as the main distributor. This change aims to improve security, simplicity, and budget allocation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CxzD6vbw--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2005","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Gmw5O3zoI","title":"QUIC Server Preview Branch Available for Testing and Feedback","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/04/16/quic-server-preview/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/quic-server-preview-branch-available-for-testing-and-feedback-gmw5o3zoi","summary":"OpenSSL has released a feature preview for their QUIC server functionality and is seeking feedback from the community. The preview is available for download and testing, but is not yet fully implemented and is not intended for production use. The official support for server-side QUIC functionality is expected to be delivered in OpenSSL 3.4.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"dx6xMYwUq","title":"OpenSSL Is Hiring","url":"https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2024/05/26/openssl-is-hiring/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/openssl-is-hiring-dx6xmywuq","summary":"OpenSSL is hiring a mid-level engineer to join their team. The position is remote and the responsibilities include contributing to the development of the OpenSSL toolkit, collaborating on secure software solutions, and maintaining technical documentation. Solid C programming experience and knowledge of network programming concepts are required. To apply, send your resume to jobs@openssl.org.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["livebook","clearpathrobotics","mikefisher","ballerina","dev_channel"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","kloss_xyz","ryolu_","felixrieseberg"],"similar":[{"id":"livebook","handle":"livebook","name":"Livebook","is_squad":false,"x":-4.1819,"y":-3.0412,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":21,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/136b9283700045c1ae25add759b7a44e","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.139174,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author